The Community Index: A More Comprehensive Approach to Assessing Scholarly Impact (Submitted to the Lancet Regional Health-Americas)
=======
 The Community Index (comm-index) is a new research metric introduced to address the limitations of traditional citation-based measures like the h-index, which only quantifies how often a scholar’s work has been cited without capturing the diversity, collaboration, and interdisciplinary nature of modern research
